  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Toluene is oxidised to benzaldehyde in presence of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> /acetic anhydride,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math></p><p>Toluene is converted to&nbsp;benzylidene diacetate&nbsp;and&nbsp;hydrolysis reaction of benzylidene diacetate&nbsp;gives benzaldehyde.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9edbce60-686a-4097-85d4-4bea5da15ff4-image.png\" style=\"width: 550px; height: 175px;\" /></p>",
